| `canary.scratch_root` | string | `.canary` | a path with no `..` part: relative to the checkout and ignored by git with nothing tracked under it, or absolute; never under the system temporary directory | `scripts/canary.py`, which takes `KEEL_CANARY_SCRATCH` over it | Moves where the canary renders its projects, their logs and its snapshot of the checkout. Read only in the template repository; absent, the canary writes `[using default] canary.scratch_root = ".canary"` to stderr. A refused value is exit 14, before anything renders. Run paths and answer-set-derived outputs are confined to this root before a run is replaced; escapes exit CONFIG. | the audit's scratch, which is a temporary directory `scripts/audit_project.py` removes | always |
